<title>USA: Andover Togs files plan to pay unsecured claims.</title>
<headline>Andover Togs files plan to pay unsecured claims.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Andover Togs Inc and its subsidiaries said on Wednesday they filed a joint plan of reorganization under which they would pay 100 percent of the principal amount of unsecured claims.</p>
<p>The amount would be paid over a five-year period, with interest.</p>
<p>The reorganization plan must be approved by Bankruptcy Court and the companies' creditors.</p>
<p>Andover, which makes children's clothing, filed a petition under Chapter 11 of the U.S. Bankruptcy Code in March 1996.</p>
<p>	  ((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
